post_install() {
  cat<<EOF

The YeetMouse service starts by itself whenever the driver loads.
Add each user of the GUI to the 'yeetmouse' group, then log out and in:

  sudo usermod -a -G yeetmouse <username>

Load the driver now with 'sudo modprobe yeetmouse', or reboot.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat<<EOF

Please add new users to 'yeetmouse' group

  sudo usermod -a -G yeetmouse <username>

Reboot your system, so changes will take effect..

EOF
}